ecm: include DSA tag_8021q metadata for bridged TCP/UDP rules

A bridged lan3 to
phy1-ap0 connection resolves to NSS interfaces 1 and 32, but patch 0027
skips DSA VLAN metadata for is_routed=0. Apply the same per-side DSA lookup
to bridged connections. The existing helper leaves non-DSA interfaces,
non-tag_8021q switches and VLAN-aware bridges alone. Existing VLAN rule
fields remain protected by the per-side NOT_CONFIGURED checks.

Observed: new wired-to-WiFi iperf control flows stall with ECM enabled,
while new flows with ECM IPv4 stopped complete. This motivates the patch
and the correction restored accelerated IPv4 bridging. IPv6 is compile-only
until a separate runtime test. No change to bridge/routed rule flags.

